{title: Drops Of Jupiter}
{artist: Train Pat Monahan}
{key: C}

{c: Verse 1}
[C]Now that shes back,        in the atmosphere
With [G]drops of Jupiter,        in her [F]hair, hey, hey
She [C]acts like summer,        and walks like rain
[G]Reminds me that theres,        [F]time to change, hey, hey
[C]Since the return from,        her stay on the moon
She [G]listens like spring,        and she [F]talks like June, hey, hey
[G]Tell me, did you sail,        across the [D]sun
Did you make it to the Milky,        [F]Way to see the lights all faded
[C]And that heaven is overrated,        [G]Tell me, did you fall
for a shooting [D]star,        [Dm]One without a permanent scar
And did you miss me while you were,        [F]looking for yourself out there
[C]Now that shes back from,        her soul vacation
[G]Tracing her way through the,        [F]constellation, hey, hey
She [C]checks out Mozart,        while she does tae-bo
Re [G]minds me that theres,        [F]time to grow, hey, hey
[G]Now that shes back,        in the [D]atmosphere
Im afraid that she might,        [F]think of me as plain ol Jane
Told a story about a man,        [C]who is too afraid
to fly so he never did land,        [G]Tell me, did the wind sweep you
off your [D]feet,        Did you finally get the [F]chance
to dance along the light of day,        And [C]head back to the Milky Way
And [G]tell me,        did Venus blow your [D]mind
[Dm]Was it everything,        you wanted to find
And did you miss me,        while you were [F]looking
for yourself out there,        Can you imagine no [G]love,
pride, deep-fried chicken,        Your [D]best friend always
sticking up for you even,        when I know you are wrong
Can you imagine no [F]first dance,        freeze dried romance
five-hour phone conversation,        The best soy latte that
you ever had... and [C]me,        [G]Tell me, did the wind
sweep you off your [D]feet,        Did you finally get the
[F]chance to dance along the light of day,        And [C]head back to the Milky Way
